Keep the standalone daemon-thread test independent of libc.

thr_daemon_exit_standalone checks that a process can exit while a daemon
thread is still running. It uses direct syscalls, supplies its own assembly
bzero, and links with -nostartfiles -nodefaultlibs to avoid libc.

GCC recognizes bzero as a builtin and can replace a call with memset.
We reproduced this with GCC 16 even at -O0: the replacement produces an
undefined reference to memset because the test provides only bzero and
does not link libc. This transformation predates GCC 16; it is not evidence
of a new GCC 16 compiler regression.

Disable only the bzero builtin for this test so that the call reaches its
own implementation, preserving the test's independence from libc.

Background on GCC's bzero-to-memset transformation:
https://gcc.gnu.org/legacy-ml/gcc-patches/2017-06/msg00530.html
Documentation of the per-function -fno-builtin option:
https://gcc.gnu.org/onlinedocs/gcc/C-Dialect-Options.html#index-fno-builtin

diff --git a/memcheck/tests/solaris/Makefile.am b/memcheck/tests/solaris/Makefile.am
--- a/memcheck/tests/solaris/Makefile.am
+++ b/memcheck/tests/solaris/Makefile.am
@@ -200,4 +200,5 @@
 mmapobj_bssonly_so_CFLAGS = $(AM_CFLAGS) -fPIC
 mmapobj_bssonly_so_LDFLAGS = -nostartfiles -nodefaultlibs -shared
 
+thr_daemon_exit_standalone_CFLAGS = $(AM_CFLAGS) -fno-builtin-bzero
 thr_daemon_exit_standalone_LDFLAGS = -nostartfiles -nodefaultlibs
